  "scope": "Complete unchanged HerbCleanListener, PotionMixingListener, UnfinishedPotion, FinishedPotion, Herbs, GenericPotion, HerblorePulse, GrindingItem, SkillPulse, Pulse, Quests and IntType, compiled with Kotlin 1.8.20/JDK 11 against the pinned ConstLib 1.4.28 artifact. Player, Item (with declared names and a slot the driver sets), the inventory (a map of amounts: containsItem compares the amount held, a removal succeeds when at least the amount is held, an addition always succeeds), the level, quest stages, attributes, lock, sendMessage, the packet dispatch's sendMessage, replaceSlot, rewardXP, addExperience, playAudio, animate, hasRequirement (true for the quests a case lists), Consumables.getConsumableById (a case's declared ids) and PulseManager.run (which records the pulse's potion and amount, calls its start() and keeps it) are recording adapters whose results come from declared case state; they are service inputs, not ports. QuestRepository.isComplete is the adapter's 'stage >= 100', the original's comparison for a registered quest. isQuestComplete, requireQuest, sendSkillDialogue, SkillDialogueBuilder, StringUtils.formatDisplayName, the Skills constants, the SkillDialogue constants with forLength, the BREWMASTER constant and SkillcapePerks.isActive are pinned text spliced into adapter shells; RandomFunction's two random methods are adapters with the original bodies whose RANDOM.nextInt is the case's next declared draw reduced into the bound. SkillDialogueHandler is an adapter that records open() with its type and items and keeps create/getAll overridable: its display, buttons and amount prompts are not covered. The driver calls the one 'clean' handler with an item of the id and slot an operation names, a use-with handler through a declared lookup (the pair as used, then flipped), not InteractionListeners, and SkillPulse.pulse() and stop() of the pulse the last run kept, not Pulse.update(): nothing here establishes on which ticks the pulse runs, only the delay it leaves. No live world, original Container/Skills arithmetic, option dispatch, dialogue interpreter or item definition behaviour is established by this corpus.",
